data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/m1-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission m1 summary: greet, tested — campaign-met\\n\\n## Mission criteria and verification\\n\\nAll three stated criteria verified by fetching dev's branch\\n(`refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`, HEAD `19ff080e0761bf4c2475025194579b5afadd3cf3`)\\nand inspecting/testing it myself — not by trusting the report:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` exists; `greet(name)` returns `\\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"` — verified by reading the file on the branch.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` exists and covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`) — verified by reading the file on the branch.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` run from the repo root of a clean detached worktree of the branch: `Ran 2 tests ... OK`, exit code 0.\\n\\n## Campaign course\\n\\n- d002 dispatched to dev with the full task and acceptance criteria.\\n- dev replied with the implementation (`c140f0e`, `19ff080`), 2 tests passing.\\n- Reply judged against the fetched branch: code correct, tests pass, tree differs from base.\\n- Reply accepted (`accept dev`); no rework rounds needed.\\n\\n## Outcome\\n\\ncampaign-met — every stated criterion is satisfied.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_25","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787694368,"id":"chatcmpl-c3675604722344f9b60f3dfa53f4501c","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

